event: response.function_call_arguments.done
data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":1906,"item_id":"fc_0cb2e64a7e5bd60c016adb44a8c1508191a8ffebc63d3d8ce0","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"inference\":\"R001\",\"packet_sha256\":\"ff875c5987601fdabc380ede3338afaa4bdc4f3b13f5b6f60ca992f1d698bab1\",\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Fresh mathematical review limited to the complete supplied packet.json and the declared Yui Audit A, self-containment, and format rules read for this task. I treated H001, H002, M001, and M002 as the only conditional mathematical inputs; I did not inspect or rely on source proofs, other inference bodies, old reviews, or external task material. This review does not certify carrier identity, canonical hash binding, transmitted-material readback, or source fidelity. The first unsupported implication is in S001: q>dim_H(E) implies H^q(E)=0. The only dimension theorem input M001 supplies the opposite-side implication d<dim_H(A) => H^d(A)=∞. The asserted threshold implication is neither a direct input nor proved locally. Acceptance stops there; later gaps are diagnostic only.\",\"checks\":{\"inputs\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The listed graph inputs are H001 (E nonempty), H002 (E compact), M001 (the stated lower-dimension threshold implication with Borel extended-metric and NNReal hypotheses), and M002 (the stated countable-sum integral identity with countability and AEMeasurability hypotheses). They are the only premises credited in this packet-only review. This is not source-fidelity verification.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/0\",\"/inputs/1\",\"/inputs/2\",\"/inputs/3\",\"/inference/inputs\"]},\"argument\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"First unsupported implication: S001 asserts the Hausdorff-dimension threshold implication q>dim_H(E) => H^q(E)=0, without an input for it or a local proof. M001 states only d<dim_H(A) => H^d(A)=∞. Consequently the covering-cost argument's starting point is unsupported. Independently, S003 later invokes the general Lipschitz-image dimension inequality and the theorem that [0,1] has Hausdorff dimension 1; neither is among the inputs nor proved locally. Other standard measure/content steps in S002 are also asserted rather than fully derived, but they occur after the first gap.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inputs/2/statement\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\"]},\"dependency_accounting\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The actual prose uses substantive unlisted results. At S001 it uses the upper-side Hausdorff dimension threshold implication. At S003 it uses the Lipschitz image dimension inequality and the nonempty-interior dimension theorem (plus the interval dimension conclusion). A calculation-policy entry permitting specified product-metric calculations cannot import any of these results. M001 and M002 do not supply them.\",\"locations\":[\"/logic/calculations/0\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/inference/applications\"]},\"output\":{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"The prose claims both inequalities and then equality for dim_H(E×I), but its conclusion is not established because the upper-bound argument already has an unsupported premise and the D=0 lower-bound branch imports unproved results. Thus the target statement is identifiable, but derivation of the exact output is not verified.\",\"locations\":[\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\"]},\"scope\":{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"The argument describes branches for n=0, D=0, and D>0 and says it combines the resulting bounds, but the packet does not give a complete formal account of quantifier introduction/discharge for the arbitrary exponents, scales, covers, and error tolerances. In particular, S002's arbitrary cover and epsilon estimates are used to claim a content infimum bound without a complete local derivation. No independent scope defect is needed to establish the earlier failure.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/locals/2\",\"/inference/locals/3\",\"/inference/locals/5\",\"/inference/locals/6\",\"/inference/locals/7\",\"/inference/locals/8\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\"]},\"applicability\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"M001 is bound in S002 to E and an NNReal coercion of s with 0<s<D; its stated Borel extended-metric and NNReal conditions are asserted to hold for Euclidean space but not fully documented beyond that assertion. M002 is bound to the countable index and restricted Lebesgue setup; the AEMeasurability claim is asserted in the application record, but its proof is only the prose assertion that the summands are constants times indicators of open intervals. More importantly, neither M application supplies S001's upper threshold implication or S003's Lipschitz-image/interval-dimension results. No other M/E application is recorded.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/2/source_contract\",\"/inputs/3/source_contract\",\"/inference/applications/0\",\"/inference/applications/1\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\"]},\"statement_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"The packet gives a concise target statement and states the needed product metric in the proof, but the output does not itself spell out the product space/metric convention. More critically for the argument's claimed contents, the precise Hausdorff measure/content conventions used in S001–S002 are introduced in prose rather than supplied as definitions or direct inputs; S002 refers to a pinned formula not included in the packet. These omissions prevent complete independent interpretation of all asserted intermediate claims.\",\"locations\":[\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/logic/primitives\"]},\"object_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The prose contains mathematical objects and operations not fully accounted for by the declarations/inventories. In particular S003 introduces a map p and uses the Lipschitz-image theorem without a local declaration for p; S002 uses restricted Lebesgue measure, indicators, lintegrals, and Hausdorff content formula objects not declared among primitives, definitions, or locals. Several locals are declared but their claimed existence/basis is not proved, e.g. the zero-diameter replacement cover and arbitrary product-cover constructions. An inventory omission alone is not the first substantive gap, but object closure is not established.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/locals\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/logic/primitives\",\"/definitions\"]},\"dependency_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Reverse-mapping factual uses to grounds reveals unlisted substantive theorem uses: the q>dim threshold implication in S001, the Lipschitz image dimension inequality in S003, and the interval dimension theorem in S003. The first of these is an unsupported implication in the actual argument. M001 only provides the opposite threshold direction; M002 concerns interchange of countable sums and integrals.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/inputs/2/statement\",\"/inputs/3/statement\"]},\"packet_replay\":{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"I read the entire supplied packet.json (448 lines) and the relevant declared Yui rules in this same interaction. This is not an execution through an independently attested fresh carrier, and I cannot verify carrier identity, isolation, canonical hash binding, or transmitted-material readback from the available tools. I therefore do not claim a fresh-carrier replay PASS. Mathematical boundary: this packet alone plus the declared review procedure; no source proofs or other mathematical task materials were used.\",\"locations\":[\"/packet_sha256\",\"/warning\"]}},\"findings\":[{\"location\":\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"kind\":\"unsupported_implication\",\"premises\":\"The packet supplies M001: if d<dim_H(A), then H^d(A)=∞; S001 also describes Hausdorff dimension as a critical exponent.\",\"conclusion\":\"For q>dim_H(E), H^q(E)=0.\",\"mathematical_basis\":\"The conclusion is the opposite-side threshold theorem, not the result stated in M001. A critical-exponent description alone, without a full definition and a local proof of the required monotonicity/threshold implication, does not discharge it. No other input or local derivation establishes it.\",\"first_unsupported\":true},{\"location\":\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"kind\":\"additional_unproved_theorem_uses\",\"premises\":\"H001 and the stated product projection construction.\",\"conclusion\":\"A 1-Lipschitz map cannot increase Hausdorff dimension; dim_H([0,1])=1 by the cited nonempty-interior theorem.\",\"mathematical_basis\":\"Neither theorem is a listed input or proved locally in the packet. These are later diagnostics, not the first gap.\"}]}}"}

